    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d726">

                <pb facs="0769" n="667" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg667"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11/1694: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-03-28T16:00:00+08:00">March 28, 1933—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 28—5:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>286. British Legation has now received instructions and drafted note to Foreign
                    Office refusing to assent to a further postponement of the Boxer Indemnity
                    payments. Italian Legation still without instructions. I am drafting note of
                    refusal to be submitted by telegraph for Peck<anchor n="47" xml:id="d726-f1"/>
                    to deliver to the Foreign Office immediately upon receipt of knowledge that
                    Italian Legation has instructions to make similar reply.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d726-f1" n="47" xml:id="d726-f1-content">
                <p>Willys R. Peck, Consul General at Nanking; also Counselor of Legation in
                    China.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
